; Sprites: barbed bars (4 frames), spiral disc (4 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $AC00+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Frames 0-3 look like a double horizontal bar with spikes (barbed wire)
; changing shape; frames 4-7 look like a round disc with a spiral, turning. Used by entity definitions $60 $61 $64 in
; rooms $1A $1B $1E $25 $36.
@label=SpritesBarbedSpiral
